  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Quà sol habenas laxat, &amp; igneas</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Currus relinquens Oceano abditur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Verum Trìones quà Lycaonius</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Auriga noƈtu Strymonios regit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Septem, propinquas magnanima aspicit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Turres Geneua, &amp; six stadiis tribus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Distans: Draconis qualia Martij,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Fortisque Victor Gerionis pedé</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Metatus olim est alite, ludicra</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Quum plura campis sanxit Olympicis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Hic fròndet arbos, quà graciles tibi.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Prabebit umbras, &amp; tepidi grauem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Refringet astum solis. Et hic casa est</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Quà tectus imbre, &amp; rabiem Africi,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Notisque temnes nymbiferi minas,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Si forte calo turbiduli fremant.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Et si salubrem hic me dare insseris</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Cœnam parata est. Protinus, ò, seni,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Cum Zastrissello sume Paludium,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Et cum Rosetis Leƈtiolum, haud locus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Permittit arƈtus iungere nunc tibi</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Plures amicos. Non Saliaria</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Mensis reponam fercula grandibus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Non insuetas delicias neque,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Quas luxus ex lex, turpis &amp; æquora:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Per cunƈta quærit lautitias gula.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Qua uina colles dulcia proximi</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Ferunt, &amp; herba nescius hadulus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29">
      <i>Pullasque iamiam grandior, &amp; suo</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Scan has show-through and a cut-off catchword at the right edge; the verse lines are partly blurred, especially the words "Trìones", "Zastrissello", "hadulus" and "fremant", which are uncertain. The final catchword "Pifcet" is only partly visible and is given as read.</notes>
